# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# There is deliberately NO `/* /index.html 200` catch-all. Every client route is
# prerendered to its own dist/<path>/index.html by the `portfolio-seo` plugin
# (from ROUTES + UNLISTED_ROUTES in src/site.config.ts), so Pages serves them as
# real static files. A blanket SPA fallback would also answer genuinely unknown
# URLs with HTTP 200 — a "soft 404" that search engines index as a real page.
# Without it, anything unmatched falls through to dist/404.html with a proper 404
# status, and the client router renders the NotFound route inside that shell.
#
# Note: Pages does NOT honour a `200` rewrite here outside that catch-all. A rule
# like `/learnings/* /index.html 200` does not rewrite — the bare path becomes a
# redirect to `/` and nested paths 404. Hence prerendered files, not rewrites.
#
# These two were client-side <Navigate> redirects; as real 301s they cost one
# less round trip and pass the signal to crawlers.
/learnings              /stats   301
/learnings/leetcode     /stats   301
